SteerTTS edge native runtime - third-party notices (the C++ front end ports the Python edge front end; the
model files it reads come from huggingface.co/WhissleAI/steer-tts-edge)

* front/cmudict.lex is derived from the CMU Pronouncing Dictionary (Copyright (C) 1993-2015 Carnegie Mellon
  University; BSD-style license, see http://www.speech.cs.cmu.edu/cgi-bin/cmudict).
* front/gru.npz is an int8 re-encoding of the g2p_en grapheme-to-phoneme model weights (Copyright 2019 Kyubyong
  Park and Jongseok Kim; Apache License, Version 2.0, http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). Changes: weights
  quantized to int8 per row with fp16 scales, numpy decoder (steertts_edge/edge_front/gru_np.py).
* steertts_edge/vocoder.py re-implements the Vocos architecture (ConvNeXt backbone + iSTFT head; Copyright (c) 2023
  Charactr Inc.; MIT License, https://github.com/gemelo-ai/vocos), and vocoder.safetensors is derived from the
  charactr/vocos-mel-24khz weights (MIT License).
* steertts_edge/edge_front/normnum.py ports g2p_en's normalize_numbers, which comes from keithito/tacotron
  text/numbers.py (Copyright (c) 2017 Keith Ito; MIT License); edge_front/tok.py ports regular expressions of NLTK's
  TweetTokenizer and edge_front/hetero.py is derived from decisions of NLTK's averaged-perceptron tagger (NLTK:
  Apache License, Version 2.0).
* steertts_edge/edge_front/numwords.py: inflect_words() ports the number_to_words logic of inflect (Copyright (c)
  Jason R. Coombs and contributors; MIT License, https://github.com/jaraco/inflect). cardinal() / ordinal() are an
  independent implementation written to match num2words' English output (no num2words code is included).
* native/front/ holds the same front end data as front/ (CMUdict entries, the int8 g2p_en GRU, heteronym and Unicode
  tables) re-encoded for the C++ runtime; the notices above apply to it unchanged. onnx/ holds the acoustic model and
  vocoder (same weights as the safetensors) as ONNX graphs.
* Model weights (acoustic, vocoder, voices) and code: see LICENSE (code, weights and voices CC BY-NC 4.0 + Whissle terms).
